1. A wearable device that vibrates or emits gentle sounds at scheduled times to remind users of tasks;
2. A smart mirror that displays visual reminders and task lists when the user looks into it;
3. An AI-powered voice assistant that learns routines and proactively reminds users of tasks in a conversational way;
4. A photo-based reminder app where users take pictures of objects tied to tasks, and the app sends notifications when those objects are nearby;
5. A connected pillbox that syncs with a calendar and sends reminders to take medication or complete health-related tasks;
6. A wall-mounted digital family board where household members can add and view shared tasks, with color-coded alerts for urgency.
